This was a pre-existing, world-famous hit by Queen. The studio (Paramount) had to *rent* it. They paid a fee for the right to use it in the movie. They do *not* own it. If they wanted to use it again in a sequel 20 years later, they'd have to pay Queen's estate all over again. **The key takeaway:** The music industry is built on *renting* famous songs, not selling them. The owners of those songs want to keep collecting checks for decades. A "forever" deal would cut off that future income, so they almost never agree to it for their biggest hits. Does that clear up the confusion?
